Layered licensing
=================

This repository mixes hardware design data with plain code and
documentation, so licensing is split into two layers:

Layer 1 — Board design content: CERN-OHL-P-2.0 (see LICENSE.BOARD)
------------------------------------------------------------------
Applies to ALL hardware design files and design documentation:

  kicad/stm32h743-coreboard-revc/            (whole project directory)
    *.kicad_sch, *.kicad_pcb, *.kicad_pro, *.kicad_sym,
    coreboard.pretty/*.kicad_mod, fp-lib-table, sym-lib-table,
    revc.netlist
  bom/*.csv                                  (public bill of materials)
  pinmap/*.md                                (pin-map / design-reference
                                              documentation)

These are the hardware design and its documentation in the sense of the
CERN Open Hardware Licence. CERN-OHL-P-2.0 is a permissive licence; the
full text (authoritative copy from https://ohwr.org/cern_ohl_p_v2.txt)
is shipped verbatim in LICENSE.BOARD.

Layer 2 — Code and repository metadata: Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE.SCRIPTS)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Applies to verification/packaging code and repository-level documents:

  tools/*.py                                 (verification scripts)
  README.md, LICENSE, LICENSE.BOARD, LICENSE.SCRIPTS

The full Apache License 2.0 text (authoritative copy from
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt) is shipped verbatim in
LICENSE.SCRIPTS.

Rule of thumb
-------------
If a file describes the board (schematic, PCB, symbols, footprints,
project config, netlist, BOM, pin maps) it is under CERN-OHL-P-2.0.
If it is a program or repo housekeeping content (scripts, README,
licence files) it is under Apache-2.0. Individual files may carry their
own SPDX identifier; where a file states a licence explicitly, that
statement wins.

Third-party property
--------------------
Vendor datasheets referenced by the design documents (ISSI
IS42S16160J, Winbond W9825G6KH) remain the property of their respective
owners. They are deliberately NOT redistributed in this repository;
obtain them from the vendors' official channels (see README.md,
"Disclosures"). The custom footprint coreboard.pretty/
Texas-VSON-7-HR.kicad_mod carries its own public provenance attribution
(LSF open library / TI datasheet) inside the file and is licensed as
board content under Layer 1.
